{"id": "wwdc2019-806", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/806", "wordCount": 3491, "segments": [{"start": 10.0, "text": "Hi. I'm Jay."}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "I'm a designer on the Siri and"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "Shortcuts team."}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "And today, we'll be talking"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "about how to design great"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "shortcuts for your apps."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "We're going to cover three main"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "topics today."}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "First, I'll talk about looking"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "at all the use cases of your"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "app, and deciding which ones"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "might make sense as shortcuts."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "Then, I'll talk about how to"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "make these shortcuts"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "discoverable in your apps."}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "And, finally, I'll walk through"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "how to design a great Siri"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "experience for the new"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "interactive capabilities of"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "shortcuts in iOS 13."}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "Now, stepping back for a moment,"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "shortcuts in general are a great"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "way to bring your app's"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "functionality in front of more"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "users in more places in the OS."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "So, let's take a look at the"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "places where your apps'"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "shortcuts can appear to get a"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "feel for what might be useful."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "If you tell the system when the"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "user does something in your app,"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "the system can automatically"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "suggest a shortcut when it"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "predicts the user will next want"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "to do that action."}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "And, these shortcuts can appear"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "in lock screen and search."}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "Here, this shortcut lets you"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "quickly start a guided workout,"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "you usually do at this time of"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "day."}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "If a user adds a shortcut to"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "Siri, by assigning it a custom"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "phrase, they can invoke it at"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "any time with their voice."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "Here, the shortcut lets them"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "order their usual dinner."}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "In one quick confirmation step,"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "the user can get some great"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "Mediterranean food."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "Another great use for shortcuts"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "with Siri is getting information"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "hands- and eyes-free."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "So, to your HomePod, if you have"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "a transit app shortcut, you can"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "say, Hey Siri, bus schedule."}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "And, Siri will speak out the bus"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "schedule information from your"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "And, you can also incorporate"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "your app's functionality as part"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "of a multi-step shortcut."}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "Here, the shortcut handles your"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "evening routine, ordering soup"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "in time for your arrival home,"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "playing your favorite music for"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "your car ride, and showing the"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "fastest directions."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "So, looking at these examples,"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "we can see that shortcuts are"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "great for accelerating"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "frequently used, useful actions"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "your app can do."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "Presenting information at a"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "glance, or with your voice, or"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "as building blocks for powerful"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "multi-step shortcuts, where your"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "app can work alongside others."}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "We introduced Siri shortcut"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "suggestions in iOS 12, so look"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "back at past sessions for more"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "information on how to develop"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "great shortcuts to be"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "automatically suggested on lock"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "screen and search."}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "Today, I'm going to focus on how"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "to make shortcuts to take"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "advantage of the new Siri"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "capabilities in iOS 13."}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "We're going to walk through how"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "to prioritize the features in"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "your app that might make for"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "good Siri shortcuts."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "To do that, let's take a look at"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "one of our favorite apps,"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "SoupChef, which lets you order a"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "wide variety of soups for pickup"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "or delivery."}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "Let's walk through the design"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "process for making a SoupChef"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "shortcut."}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "List out all the things that"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "your app can do."}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "When doing so, start thinking"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "about things that a user might"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "want to repeat with their voice."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "So, with SoupChef, you can do"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "things like browse the menu of"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "soups."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "Order a soup."}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "Check your order status, or view"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "past orders."}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "Let's take a look at some of"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "these features one by one."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "Browsing a menu is a very visual"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "activity that requires a lot of"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "structured information that"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "won't translate well to voice."}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "It requires scrolling, tapping,"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "and navigating."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "And, it provides information"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "that isn't likely to change from"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "invocation to invocation."}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "And, it's more of a means to an"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "end, and not a valuable action"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "in and of itself."}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "So, this might not be a good"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "candidate for a shortcut."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "Checking an order status could"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "be something a user might want"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "to do with their voice, getting"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "a quick summary of information"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "from Siri."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "But, it's also only applicable"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "for a narrow window of time,"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "right after a user's ordered"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "something."}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "So, this is something that you"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "could consider allowing users to"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "turn into a shortcut, but maybe"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "only if your delivery periods"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "are long, or have multiple"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "phases."}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "And viewing past orders is nice"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "to have, but I don't know about"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "you, I'm not regularly checking"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "that."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "So, not a great shortcut."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "Ordering a soup is a very"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "valuable activity."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "In fact, the most important"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "activity of your app."}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "And, you can imagine it being"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "repeatable if a user has a"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "favorite soup."}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "So, let's call this a pretty"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "good candidate for a shortcut."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "So, in summary, a great use for"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "shortcuts will be something that"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "is valuable, or interesting to"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "repeat."}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "Doable with your voice by not"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "relying on visuals or tapping."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "And, invokable in many contexts."}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "So, the shortcut isn't just"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "applicable during a small window"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "of time."}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "So, now that we know that we"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "want users to be able to reorder"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "soup with shortcuts, let's take"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "a look at how we might make that"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "discoverable in your app."}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "We provide a standard Add to"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "Siri button, that makes it easy"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "for users to see what features"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "in your app can be turned into a"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "Siri shortcut."}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "But use it thoughtfully."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "Don't do this, where you put an"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "Add to Siri button on every item"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "on your main menu."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "As beautiful as the button is on"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "its own, repeating it like this"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "looks ugly, and it's not really"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "relevant here."}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "The user's probably just trying"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "to make an order in the first"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "place."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "And, these buttons are getting"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "in the way."}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "And, these could be items that"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "the user has never ordered"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "before. So, it doesn't make sense to"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "suggest reordering them just"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "yet. Instead, look at opportunities"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "where you can present it in a"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "focused UI, where you have a"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "clear signal that a user might"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "want to repeat something."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "For example, it might be better"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "to show an Add to Siri button"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "right after a user has ordered"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "something."}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "The logic being, if a user's"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "found it good enough to order"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "before, the user's more likely"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "to want to order it again."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "And, you're not interrupting"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "anything a user's trying to do."}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "They just finished their order,"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "so this is a good opportunity."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "To make the Add to Siri button"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "fit in to your app's visual"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "appearance even better, you can"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "now customize the corner radius"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "of the button."}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "And, you can have its appearance"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "automatically change based on"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "the user's light or dark mode"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "preference."}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "Now, if you've tried really"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "hard, like really hard, and the"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "button's visual style doesn't"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "fit into your app, you can make"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "your own button. But, you should replicate all of"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "Add to Siri's functionality."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "The standard Add to Siri button"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "shows the user's shortcut phrase"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "once configured."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "And, this is a good way to remind the user what they can"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "say to run the shortcut."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "Tapping on it will reveal a"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "standard sheet which allows the"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "user to edit or delete the"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "shortcut."}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "If you want a centralized place"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "in your app where you list all"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "your shortcuts, it might be too"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "much to have the Add to Siri"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "button on every row, like we saw"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "earlier."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "So, instead, you're free to use"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "standard UIKit elements."}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "Just make sure that when a user"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "sets up a shortcut, just like"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "the Add to Siri button, you show"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "the phrase the user has set up"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "the shortcut with."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "Tapping on it should also reveal"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "the sheet, where you can edit or"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "delete the shortcut."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "So, let's get back to users"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "setting up the shortcut for the"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "first time."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "Once the user taps on the Add to"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "Siri button, they'll see the Add"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "to Siri sheet, where the user"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "can choose what phrase to use to"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "invoke the shortcut."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "In iOS 13, your app can pre-fill"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "a shortcut of your own choosing."}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "And, most users will probably"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "just assign this phrase if you"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "provide it, so make sure you"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "provide a good default."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "Order Soup is a good, short,"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "memorable phrase in this case,"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "that the user might want to"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "genuinely want to use for the"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "shortcut."}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "Let's take a look at another"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "example, and take a break from"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "soup for a while."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "Checking the bus schedule."}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "While this might look like a"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "sensible phrase, given how"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "relatively short it is, there"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "are plenty of opportunities for"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "the user to forget words, or"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "switch words around."}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "They might try to say, Look up"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "the bus schedule. Or, the bus schedule for the 35."}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "Or, just drop the \"the\""}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "altogether."}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "While Siri will do its best to"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "match these to the phrase, users"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "can still get pretty creative"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "when trying to recall longer"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "phrases."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "So, this might not be the best"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "suggested phrase."}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "Instead, keep it short, at"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "around three or fewer words."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "Try limiting it to a proper"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "noun, or just a verb and an"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "This reduces the chance that"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "users will mix up word order, or"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "use different prepositions."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "OK. A user wants to set up a"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "shortcut for ordering tomato"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "soup."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "But, what if the user wants the"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "shortcut to do something"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "slightly different every time,"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "like order a different soup."}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "In iOS 13, users can tap on the"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "cell under the Do area, and"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "customize how much information"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "is pre-baked into the shortcut"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "by simply tapping on one of the"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "fields."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "The user can choose to leave"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "certain fields blank, like the"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "type of soup itself."}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "And, when they do that, Siri can"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "ask for this missing information"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "on your app's behalf."}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "Now, ideally a shortcut has very"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "minimal interaction."}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "After all, it should accelerate"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "people to something that they do"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "frequently."}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "So, when you present the ad to"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "Siri sheet, the action should"}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "include as much information as"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "possible, to run the shortcut"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "with just one or two steps."}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "In this case, this shortcut goes"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "straight to the confirmation"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "screen, because everything is"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "already specified."}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "But, what happens when a user"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "chooses to leave everything"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "blank, and wants to specify all"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "of the details of their order in"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "an interaction with Siri?"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "Let's take a look at how we"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "might design a complete ordering"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "soup interaction with Siri."}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "Think about what information you"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "need to know in order to carry"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "out a soup request."}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "Like, the kind of soup it is."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "Whether you're ordering for"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "delivery or pick up?"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "And, if you're ordering for"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "delivery, what location are you"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "delivering to, and if you're"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "ordering for pickup, what you're"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "picking up from."}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "To start thinking about the"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "order and manner in which you"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "might collect this information,"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "you should think of your app's"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "interaction as a conversation"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "between your user and Siri."}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "And, one way to visualize this"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "conversation is with a script,"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "which is useful for quickly"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "jotting down one conversational"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "path."}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "Of course, there isn't just one"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "path you can go down."}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "You should write down all of the"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "possible paths in which the"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "conversation might go."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "For example, a user could say an"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "option that's not supported by"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "your app."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "In that case, Siri should"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "probably indicate that to the"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "user."}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "Now, handing over a book of"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "scripts might get unwieldy as a"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "design specification, so, at the"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "end of the process, you'll"}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "probably end up with something"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "more like this; a flow diagram"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "that covers all the possible"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "states and transitions within a"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "conversation."}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "Now, there are specific ways"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "that Siri can present choices,"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "and handle user input, so let's"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "dive straight into the"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "conversational patterns you have"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "at your disposal."}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "The first pattern that you have"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "is the prompt."}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "This is the most open-ended way"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "you can collect a value from the"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "user."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "You should write your prompt as"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "a question, and phrase it in a"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "way that sets the user up for a"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "well-formed response."}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "When a user says something that"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "might mean multiple things to"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "your app, you can present an"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "option list which allows the"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "user to specify which one they"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "meant."}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "This is called a disambiguation"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "prompt."}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "You can minimize disambiguation"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "prompts, which add another step"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "to your conversation, by"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "presenting an option list up"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "front."}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "Notice that the user has said"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "their shortcut phrase, Order"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "Soup, and went straight to the"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "list."}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "You should use this instead of a"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "free-form prompt if there's a"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "constrained list of options to"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "choose from."}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "Make sure your prompt dialog"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "encourages choosing from a list."}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "Questions that start with the"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "word \"which\" work really well"}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "here."}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "When using s shortcut without a"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "display, Siri will read out"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "options."}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "Like on AirPods, on HomePod, or"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "when the user says Hey Siri."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "And, Siri will read these out as"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "you would provide them in your"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "visual UI."}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "But, you can imagine that this"}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "could get verbose, especially if"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "a lot of the options are"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "similar."}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "To improve this experience, you"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "can separately specify how Siri"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "reads your options out loud, by"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "providing pronunciation hits"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "that you can add to each option."}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "Let's take a look at a slightly"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "different example."}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "The user has asked for Noodle"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "Soup."}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "And, there are two kinds."}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "Instead of saying Beef Noodle"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "Soup, or Veggie Noodle Soup, you"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "might want to just say Beef or"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "Veggie?"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "So, consider only reading out"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "the details that differentiate"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "between each item."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "Now, conversations are a two-way"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "street, so you also have to"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "account for what the user might"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "say."}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "And, the user may not use the"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "exact words that you've labeled"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "the option with."}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "To handle natural variations in"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "responses, for each option, you"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "should provide Siri with"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "synonyms that mean the same"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "thing as that option."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "So, when the user just says"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "Beef, it'll match to Beef Noodle"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "Soup."}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "When coming up with these"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "synonyms, you should also keep"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "in mind that the phrasing of"}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "your question impacts the way"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "the user may respond."}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "So, if you have a more casual"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "way of describing the options,"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "like the one with meat, or the"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "vegetarian one, you should make"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "sure that you recognize the user"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "repeating that kind of phrasing"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "back to Siri."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "If a user provides a response"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "that you want to be extra sure"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "about, like a value of"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "particularly high consequence,"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "you can provide a parameter"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "confirmation prompt."}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "But, use this judiciously, and"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "only for truly exceptional"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "cases, as this slows the user"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "down."}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "One alternative way of using a"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "parameter confirmation prompt is"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "if your app has its own logic"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "for predicting what a user might"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "want."}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "You can present your best guess"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "to the user, and they can either"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "confirm it, in which case, yay,"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "they don't have to provide"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "additional details."}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "Or, they can deny it, in which"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "case you can fall back to a more"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "open-ended prompt."}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "If you can guess what the user"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "wants, it's a great way of"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "making your shortcut interaction"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "even faster."}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "At the end of the flow, consider"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "using a confirmation prompt that"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "applies to the action as a"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "whole, particularly if the"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "action itself is of high"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "consequence."}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "In this step, you can confirm"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "all of the details of the action"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "about to be performed that's"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "relevant to the decision, like"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "price and delivery time in a"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "visual user interface that you"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "can fully customize."}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "Note that for actions in the"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "ordering category, the system"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "requires the user to confirm."}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "So, make sure, if you fall under"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "that category, you provide a"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "great confirmation experience."}, {"start": 878.0, "text": "But, remember that your shortcut"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "can be run by a user not looking"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "at a screen, so you should"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "provide dialog for voice-only"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "experiences."}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "In this case, we provide"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "additional dialog to help the"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "user make a choice."}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "The purpose of this additional"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "dialog is to provide information"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "that can't otherwise be"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "displayed in a visual user"}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "interface."}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "So, think of this extra dialog"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "as a spoken equivalent of the"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "most important information you"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "would otherwise draw in a display."}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "Finally, your response."}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "Siri will indicate the status of"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "the action."}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "You can provide a visual UI"}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "summary here to describe"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "additional details, like who's"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "going to be delivering your soup, and the latest estimated"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "delivery time."}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "Notice that we just say, \"OK."}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "Ordered\" here, because we're"}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "using a display to show the"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "additional information."}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "For voice-only experiences, you"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "should specify a more"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "descriptive dialog."}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "And, again, think of this extra"}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "dialog as a spoken equivalent of"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "the most important information"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "of the response UI you would"}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "draw on a display."}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "When you're thinking about your"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "confirmation and response"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "dialog, you should keep in mind"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "that you'll need to select a"}, {"start": 950.0, "text": "category for your shortcut."}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "When you define your shortcut in"}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "Xcode, select the category that"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "is the closet match to your"}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "shortcut's functionality."}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "In our SoupChef case, it's"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "pretty clear that the order"}, {"start": 960.0, "text": "category fits the bill."}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "In confirmation prompts, Siri"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "will provide the question"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "itself, based on the category"}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "you select."}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "So, don't include a question as"}, {"start": 972.0, "text": "part of the confirmation dialog"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "you customize, highlighted in"}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "white here."}, {"start": 979.0, "text": "In response dialog, Siri will"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "provide a status that is"}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "appropriate to the category."}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "Your custom dialog gets appended"}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "to the end of the dialog Siri"}, {"start": 986.0, "text": "provides."}, {"start": 990.0, "text": "Voice interactions should also"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "be as robust as possible, to"}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "avoid forcing the user to open"}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "the app to continue manually."}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "For example, you should provide"}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "clear error messages if a"}, {"start": 1001.0, "text": "parameter value is invalid."}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "Siri will then automatically"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "re-prompt for that value."}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "You should also avoid getting"}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "yourself into this scenario in"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "the first place."}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "If you're presenting option"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "lists, make sure you don't"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "present any options that you"}, {"start": 1014.0, "text": "know to be invalid at runtime."}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "You should also consider"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "opportunities to dig users out"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "of holes."}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "Users may include values like"}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "delivery location in their"}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "shortcut, since it's usually"}, {"start": 1026.0, "text": "just their home, and so they get"}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "used to not saying their"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "delivery location to Siri."}, {"start": 1031.0, "text": "One day they might use the"}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "shortcut when they're far from"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "home. You should check for that case,"}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "and prompt for a different"}, {"start": 1036.0, "text": "location."}, {"start": 1037.0, "text": "And, for whatever reason, users"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "might want to continue running"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "the shortcut in your app."}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "They can tap anywhere in your UI"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "to do that."}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "So, when you present UI, keep in"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "mind that the whole area is one"}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "big button that opens your app."}, {"start": 1050.0, "text": "So, don't draw elements that"}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "look individually interactable."}, {"start": 1053.0, "text": "They can't be."}, {"start": 1055.0, "text": "Make sure that when a user does"}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "tap this area, your app opens up"}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "to the right place, with all of"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "the information the user has"}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "already provided up until that"}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "point, filled out in the app."}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "And, finally, we encourage you"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "to take time when writing"}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "dialog."}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "It's not something that you can"}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "just do a quick pass at, to have"}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "something to demo, and then"}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "leave in your final shipping product."}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "Remember, that in a voice"}, {"start": 1078.0, "text": "interaction, language is the"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "user interface."}, {"start": 1081.0, "text": "So, you should treat the words"}, {"start": 1083.0, "text": "in your Siri interaction with as"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "much respect and care as you do"}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "the pixels in your app."}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "With that said, let's walk"}, {"start": 1090.0, "text": "through a small set of"}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "guidelines."}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "Don't be overly polite or inject"}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "too much personality."}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "Users who want to customize"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "their soup will hear this"}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "non-essential dialog every time"}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "they run this shortcut, which"}, {"start": 1103.0, "text": "will get irritating."}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "When in doubt, test it."}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "Listen to Siri speak your"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "dialog."}, {"start": 1110.0, "text": "How does your dialog feel to you"}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "after the third time hearing it?"}, {"start": 1113.0, "text": "What about the 10th?"}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "If parts of it feel annoying, it"}, {"start": 1117.0, "text": "might be a good signal that you"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "should reduce the verbosity of"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "your dialog."}, {"start": 1123.0, "text": "Dialog should be concise,"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "neutral, and communicate the"}, {"start": 1126.0, "text": "type of response that you're"}, {"start": 1127.0, "text": "expecting."}, {"start": 1128.0, "text": "Don't include your app name in"}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "your dialog."}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "Your app will already be"}, {"start": 1136.0, "text": "attributed, visually, via your"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "confirmation and response UI,"}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "and occasionally via Siri's own"}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "additions. So, just take your name out."}, {"start": 1143.0, "text": "Don't worry, your brand is safe."}, {"start": 1149.0, "text": "Similarly, you shouldn't include"}, {"start": 1151.0, "text": "your user's name in your dialog."}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "Siri may at times speak the"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "user's name on HomePod to verify"}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "their identity."}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "If your app does so as well, it"}, {"start": 1159.0, "text": "might sound repetitive and"}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "annoying."}, {"start": 1162.0, "text": "So, just take your name out."}, {"start": 1167.0, "text": "Avoid using first-person"}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "pronouns, since Siri isn't"}, {"start": 1170.0, "text": "performing the action, your app"}, {"start": 1172.0, "text": "is. It's a subtle distinction, but"}, {"start": 1174.0, "text": "it's an important one."}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "By saying \"I\" or \"we\" in Siri's"}, {"start": 1177.0, "text": "voice, users might think Siri"}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "has a better understanding of"}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "your app's capabilities than it"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "does, and might try to take"}, {"start": 1183.0, "text": "follow-up actions that your app"}, {"start": 1185.0, "text": "and Siri can't understand."}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "Instead, present options"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "neutrally, using words like"}, {"start": 1193.0, "text": "\"here\" or \"there are a few options.\""}, {"start": 1198.0, "text": "So, what have we learned today?"}, {"start": 1202.0, "text": "Shortcuts are meant to elevate"}, {"start": 1204.0, "text": "your app's most repeatable"}, {"start": 1205.0, "text": "features."}, {"start": 1206.0, "text": "You should use the Add to Siri"}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "button to make sure users know"}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "what they can turn into a"}, {"start": 1212.0, "text": "shortcut from inside your app."}, {"start": 1215.0, "text": "You should make your Siri"}, {"start": 1216.0, "text": "interactions logical, concise,"}, {"start": 1218.0, "text": "and robust."}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "And, you should take extra care"}, {"start": 1222.0, "text": "when writing dialog."}]}